---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Grid from '../../components/Grid.astro';
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro';
import { ORG } from '../../consts';

/** TODO(sam): replace with the recurring-gift URL once the Givebutter plan exists. */
const GIVE_URL = ORG.social.givebutter;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Become a Lantern Keeper"
  description="Lantern Keepers give monthly, so the Florida Lantern Project can say yes to a family within the hour instead of waiting to see what comes in."
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="Lantern Keepers"
    title="The answer has to be ready before the storm has a name"
    lede="When someone calls at 9pm the night before landfall, there is no time to run a fundraiser. Either the money is already there or the answer is no."
  >
    <p class="actions"><a class="btn" href={GIVE_URL}>Give monthly</a></p>
  </Hero>

  <Section title="What a Lantern Keeper is">
    <p class="intro">
      A Lantern Keeper gives a set amount every month. That's the whole idea. It
      is unglamorous and it is the single most useful thing a supporter can do
      for a disaster relief organization.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nearly everything else we raise is episodic — a gala, a campaign, a storm
      that makes the news. But the calls don't arrive on that schedule, and the
      expensive moment is always the one before landfall, when a room has to be
      booked tonight and reimbursement is a problem for later.
    </p>
    <p>
      Monthly gifts are the reserve that lets us commit first and account
      afterwards.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="surface" title="What it pays for">
    <Grid>
      <Card title="$10 a month" meta="Readiness">
        <p>Builds toward emergency readiness kits and keeps the storm hotline staffed through a season.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="$25 a month" meta="Documentation">
        <p>Roughly a post-storm drone inspection every year — the report a family hands to an insurer, or that unlocks an SBA loan.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="$50 a month" meta="Shelter">
        <p>Several nights of emergency lodging a year for a family with nowhere to go and animals no shelter will take.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card title="$100 a month" meta="Infrastructure">
        <p>Contributes to a neighborhood weather station feeding open-source forecasting for everyone around it, not just one address.</p>
      </Card>
    </Grid>
    <p class="note">
      These are honest illustrations of what things cost us, not restricted
      designations. Gifts go to wherever the need is sharpest that month.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Why monthly beats an annual gift of the same size">
    <ul class="reasons">
      <li>
        <strong>It arrives before the storm.</strong> A December gift doesn't help
        a family evacuating in October.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>It lets us commit fast.</strong> Knowing what next month looks like
        is the difference between “we'll see what we can do” and “we've booked it.”
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>It costs almost nothing to steward.</strong> No venue, no auction,
        no printing. Close to the entire gift reaches the work.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>It makes us fundable.</strong> Grantmakers look for a stable base
        before they'll commit. Recurring donors are that base.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn" href={GIVE_URL}>Become a Lantern Keeper</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/give/donate">Prefer a one-time gift?</a>
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="surface" title="Where the money goes">
    <p>
      We publish our legal name, EIN, board, and financial filings, and we'd
      rather you check them than take our word for it.
    </p>
    <p><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/about/transparency">See our transparency page</a></p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .actions { margin-top: var(--space-md); }
  .intro { font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .note { font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-top: var(--space-md); }
  .reasons { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--space-sm); margin: var(--space-md) 0; }
  .reasons li { border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent); padding-left: var(--space-sm); max-width: var(--measure); }
  .cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-sm); margin-top: var(--space-md); }
</style>
